y better to keep** due to lower utility to opponents (cannot form any chow without T2/T3, which are gone), making it more likely to survive in the wall and possibly be discarded safely later.\n\nThus, discard T7.\n\nReason: Discarding T7 retains a slightly safer and less useful tile (T1) for completing a future pair, while removing a tile (T7) that is more commonly used in sequences and thus potentially more dangerous to hold onto in late game. Additionally, T1 has equal scarcity and better stealth for a final win.\n\nAnswer: Play T7"}
